Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a8a4f843-7c43-40d1-bff6-ec646acfbe80"],

Cell["\<\
This entry is the conformal boundary of the accelerating, rotating, dyonic \
AdS4 black hole of arXiv:2106.05571 as a three-dimensional spacetime in its \
own right -- the arena in which the Ward identities are checked and the \
conserved charges of section 3.1 are defined. It consumes \
Sol__3dL__Induced-accelerating-black-hole__ADM, which holds the boundary \
metric, the boundary gauge field, the renormalised stress tensor and the \
electric current as stored rules, and the theory scaffold \
Thr__3dL__Boundary-minimal-gauged.

The distinction between the two three-dimensional entries matters. The \
induced entry lives at a finite cutoff z = zc and its metric is an abstract \
function of the cutoff; this one lives exactly at z = 0, its metric is the \
explicit paper eq. (3.7), and it carries no radial data at all. Charges are \
integrals over a spatial slice of THIS geometry.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4a54b1b5-fa6a-4d4a-aa68-9f8ac28359ef"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sol", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "GetData", "[", "\"\<Curated/Thr__3dL__Boundary-minimal-gauged\>\"", 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bdy", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "GetData", "[", "\"\<Sol__3dL__Induced-accelerating-black-hole__ADM\>\"", 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"full", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "GetData", "[", "\"\<Sol__4dL__Accelerating-black-hole__PD\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Load", "@", "sol"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9969152376593227`*^9, 3.996915241009955*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a59017af-72fd-48d4-883d-2e9344ec0659"],

