Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Ward identities", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"51e82d2b-a4b2-47a4-8624-4c80c7b65770"],

Cell["\<\
The identities of paper eq. (3.13): the boundary current is conserved, and \
the stress tensor is conserved up to the Lorentz force exerted by the \
boundary field strength, D_i T^i_j = - j^i F_ij. The trace vanishes as well, \
which is the statement that the dual theory is conformal. All three are \
checked covariantly with the package's connection, not component by component.

A vanishing residual is only meaningful if the thing it is built from does \
not vanish on its own: the divergence of the stress tensor ALONE is checked \
to be nonzero, so the Lorentz-force identity is a genuine cancellation \
between two nonzero objects rather than a pair of empty statements.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c7a9e69c-fed1-42da-bb23-428638f3e8a2"],

