Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Conserved charges", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e6988112-4734-4c94-aea2-362d534d185b"],

Cell["\<\
Section 3.1 of the paper. The charge associated with a boundary Killing \
vector k is Q_k = Integral over Sigma_infinity of sqrt(gamma) u_i (T^i_j + \
j^i A_j) k^j, over a surface of constant barred time. The barred time is \
defined by t = tbar, phi = phibar + (Delta phi/2 pi) Omega_infinity tbar, \
with Omega_infinity fixed by paper eq. (3.16) -- it is stored in the \
four-dimensional entry's potentials rule, since the same constant appears in \
the first law.

Two simplifications make this cheap. First, sqrt(gamma) times the boundary \
lapse is just sqrt(-det g_bdy), and that is a perfect square here, so no Sqrt \
survives -- asserted below rather than hoped for. Second, u_i has only a time \
component in the barred frame, so the integrand is a single row of the mixed \
stress tensor contracted with the Killing vector.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c9e620b2-031d-4d89-b7c0-d1341f4a55ee"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

