Cell["\<\
The angular momentum is the charge of k = -(Delta phi/2 pi) d/dphi, paper eq. \
(3.19); it is independent of Omega_infinity because d/dphibar = d/dphi. The \
electric charge is the integrated charge density, eq. (3.20), and the \
magnetic charge the flux of the boundary field strength, eq. (3.21) -- for \
the latter the integral of dA over the spindle is just the difference of the \
azimuthal potential between the two poles x = -1 and x = +1. All four agree \
with the paper exactly. As with the mass, the gauge-field term in J \
integrates to zero.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fcf3c0f0-75db-423c-801f-d6a4782026f3"],

